{
 "about": "Türkiye's declared halt of trade with Israel against both states' own monthly returns. Türkiye reports exports by country of destination and Israel reports imports by country of origin, so a gap between them measures routing through third countries, not smuggling: a Turkish-made good shipped via a third country is an export to that country in Türkiye's books and an import of Turkish origin in Israel's. Figures are US dollars. A month with no Israel line in Türkiye's returns is marked reported when Türkiye reported other partners that month, so an absent line is not read as a fall to zero unless the check passed.",
